Idiot went down in to the Sanctum.  I really liked the sea of ants that the
priests generated.  I could have waded through that for thousands of moves.
But anyway, Idiot eventually found the secret door on the south wall of the
temple.  He broke in, whacked the Wizard of Yendor and the High Priest of
Moloch and found *two* Amulets of Yendor.  This was no problem, he just cast
Identify (which was at 0%) and figured out which was fake.  Then he drank
one of his c!oGL and escaped back up to 48.  He had to ditch the Candelabrum
immediately to get unburdened.  Then he started bearing the Amulet up
through the dark dungeon.

The mysterious fouce was a minor problem.  44->45, 45->45, 44->44, 43->44.

The wizard found me on level 42 (AGAIN) and I climbed to level 41 one move
later; he followed.  Idiot killed him again of level 41 as he walked.  Once
again, he saved the charges on his only wand of death.

41->41, 35->36, 36->37.

Idiot saw that good old gray unicorn on Baalz and tossed him a sapphire :).

29->29

He used his second c!oGL on the castle, and his last c!oGL on Medusa.  He
finally reached his stash on 16.  Most of the walls of the stash room had
been chewed away by umber hulks and such, but giants had provided plenty of
boulders and they formed a good replacement wall.  Idiot did some stash
swapping and had to drop the Book of the Dead to get unburdened.

So Idiot got up to Dlvl 1 and saw the engraving he had made a long time ago.
It says "GOOD LUCK".  Being an Idiot, he forgot that he wrote the message
himself, and he became awed and inspired.

Then he remembered that he had left the second magic marker (1:50) back in
his stash on 16!  The plan was to genocide cockatrices right before entering
the Astral Plane, and then wish for a cockatrice corpse and enjoy a monopoly
on stone-power.  So he jogged in his speed boots all the way back down to 16
and grabbed the marker and a few scrolls.

Then he drank the blessed smoky potion he had, but it gave no wish.  But it
didn't matter, he had a full ascension kit and his wand of wishing was
(1:3).

So he entered into the final challenge.  First was the plane of earth.  He
had brought about 7 wands of digging, and a pick-axe, but it turned out to
be unnecessary.  He used the Orb of Fate to find the portal, and it only
took about 3 digging charges to get to it.  It felt good to ditch the
pick-axe at last and get Idiot even less burdened.

Then he reached the plane of Air.  Those air elementals were surprisingly
tough.  By tough, I mean that they got Idiot's hitpoints to about 490(546).
They didn't actually threaten his life, but they were vicious.  He used a
confused b?oGD to find the portal, and levitated over to it as fast as he
could.  He teleported a few air elementals out of the way.  Once again, he
had brought lots of wands of teleportation, but only one was necessary.

The plane of fire was pretty easy.  It is kind of annoying because almsot
every turn some fiery monster steps on a fire trap and Nethack has to play
the little animation of it resisting the fire.  But that's okay, I like to
savor these moments anyway.  So Idiot used another b?oGD and just walked to
the portal, largely ignoring the monsters that were hitting him.

Then he came upon the plane of water.  He put on his water walking boots and
his oilskin cloak.  All ";" creatures were genocided so there was no threat
of instant death.  Nevertheless, Idiot clutched the amulet of life-saving
confidently to his chest.  He walked nimbly across the water, trying to
avoid the annoying bubbles.  The plane of water actually took less time than
fire.

At last, he reached the Astral Plane.  Idiot had forgot his grand plan to
genocide cockatrices and wish for cockatrice corpse etc...  He is an Idiot
after all.  But it didn't matter.  There were no cockatrices on the plane.
Status of the Guardian Angel of The Lady (neutral):  Level 17  HP 128(128)
AC -6, tame.

That was nice of The Lady; but I don't remember paying for that when we
arranged this vacation!  Idiot took off his ring of slow digestion.  Side
note: He needed *no* food in the planes.  I think he was satiated the entire
time, but he did have 10 K-rations in the bag of holding just in case.
Idiot then put on his +2 ring of increase damage and his ring of free
action.  He used telepathy to find the riders.

 Astral Layout:
Pestilence     Death       Famine

Idiot decided to go up the middle and take on Death.  He was the Envoy of
Balance after all.  So he travelled to the center, neither to the left nor
to the right.  The +2 Magicbane stunned and confused Gregg the Knight, so he
started hitting a priest of Offler (chaotic).

Status of Death (neutral): Level 36  HP 59(59)  AC -5

Idiot had MC 3, magic resistance, and reflection.  I guess if he didn't have
MR, death would have killed him.  But with MR all Death could do was take
away six maximum hitpoints (546 -> 540).  He destroyed Death once, way at
the bottom of the level, and for some reason had to destroy Death again.

He fought his way through the chaos up into the high temple.  It was the
temple of The Lady!  Monsters started fleeing him as soon as he stepped on
the threshold.  He hung out in there for a while, savoring the moment.  Then
he realized that his Guardian Angel was back at the place where he had
entered the planes.  Death was blocking the way.  He was saddened to lose
the Angel, but unwilling to risk a stupid death.  So he tamed a nearby
yellow dragon with charm monster, and named him Angel.  That was one of the
cleverest things he ever did.  So he attached a leash to Angel and brought
him up to the altar.


